                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d7291b1-021a-4cf1-bf5d-41d3b84aaf09",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f7b3008-951a-36cf-b8f4-c43575ebdffa",
                        "target_lang_word": "shameless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shameless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c083930a-baf6-3bb3-88fb-e180b7a9b595",
                                        "entry_id": "bf56cb2a-7e09-3591-97c0-ff7c3ea505e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having no shame, no guilt nor remorse over something considered wrong; immodest, brazen; unable to feel disgrace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90afda82-76b2-3c3e-9843-3da5a42b8b79",
                                        "entry_id": "bf56cb2a-7e09-3591-97c0-ff7c3ea505e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not subject to other people’s shaming or reproach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6deb1f09-f539-4c5a-b9aa-417b17fd3bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "90afda82-76b2-3c3e-9843-3da5a42b8b79",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: blameless, unblameable"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faffcb70-0a80-4e6b-bad3-164d2c272aed",
                                                "sense_id": "90afda82-76b2-3c3e-9843-3da5a42b8b79",
                                                "text": "He shall be as now nameles,\nBut he shall not be blameles,\nNor he shall not be shameles;\nFor sure he wrought amys, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1917b5b8-0d17-4331-8e9c-b5827dae35cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f7b3008-951a-36cf-b8f4-c43575ebdffa",
                        "target_lang_word": "impudent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "impudent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e89ed59d-597b-38b6-b780-089250cdb49a",
                                        "entry_id": "2da75734-0327-3c87-a411-2ab0c167988a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not showing due respect; bold-faced, impertinent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cedc9395-6c10-4a68-8a17-7aa8d2d54524",
                                                "sense_id": "e89ed59d-597b-38b6-b780-089250cdb49a",
                                                "text": "The impudent children would not stop talking in class."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fd84a35-892e-45de-bbe6-16fc2bb076d5",
                                                "sense_id": "e89ed59d-597b-38b6-b780-089250cdb49a",
                                                "text": "Sir Iohn, ſir Iohn, I am well acquainted with your maner of wrenching the true cauſe,the falſe way. It is not a confident brow, nor the throng of wordes, that come with ſuch (more then impudent) ſawcines from you, can thruſt me from a leuell conſideration, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8cd4927-875f-43d0-b037-dbbcefefe2f6",
                                                "sense_id": "e89ed59d-597b-38b6-b780-089250cdb49a",
                                                "text": "“Wickam,” retorted Mrs. Pipchin, coloring, “is a wicked, impudent, bold-faced hussy.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ae2150-91c3-47b8-a6e7-b89a573be6e3",
                                                "sense_id": "e89ed59d-597b-38b6-b780-089250cdb49a",
                                                "text": "And another asked me if I had come to get a Canadian sweetheart; and a third, one of the impudentest, most conceitedest fellows I ever did set eyes upon, nudged me, so that I spilled my coffee all over my second-best damask-silk apron—the one with bugle fringe, you know, Miss Capel—and says he, 'Is it a case of Barkis is willin'?'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed151ec1-5309-3031-bbfe-1eb154ce8e3c",
                                        "entry_id": "2da75734-0327-3c87-a411-2ab0c167988a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking modesty or shame; indelicate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6d3e1e4-3aaf-4198-bca7-6e91fc1180c0",
                                                "sense_id": "ed151ec1-5309-3031-bbfe-1eb154ce8e3c",
                                                "text": "Dian. Good my Lord,\nAske him vpon his oath, if hee do’s thinke\nHe had not my virginity.\nKin. What ſaift thou to her?\nBer. She’s impudent my Lord,\nAnd was a common gameſter to the Campe.\nDia. He do’s me wrong my Lord: If I were ſo,\nHe might haue bought me at a common price."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3b97cdb-4c5f-468a-95f5-d6f702ac0ed1",
                                                "sense_id": "ed151ec1-5309-3031-bbfe-1eb154ce8e3c",
                                                "text": "So she caught him, and kissed him, and with an impudent face, said vnto him, I haue peace offerings with me: this day haue I paid my vowes. Therefore came I forth to meete thee, diligently to seeke thy face, and I haue found thee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10884008-4ce3-4e01-9b6d-55ac9519a77e",
                                                "sense_id": "ed151ec1-5309-3031-bbfe-1eb154ce8e3c",
                                                "text": "Wine and women will make men of vnderstanding to fall away, and he that cleaueth to harlots will become impudent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
